## 3. Conservative Fair Value

Replace the current single heuristic fair value with a hybrid estimator.

Produce at least:

```ts
{
  conservativeFairValue,
  centralFairValue,
  optimisticFairValue,
  fastEstimate,
  confidence
}
```

The conservative value should use completed/inferred-sale evidence first.

Use ideas from Donut-Algorithm such as:

```text
weighted median
p40
credible active asks
```

and apply conservative penalties for:

```text
falling market
high volatility
high visible supply
low confidence
stale history
```

Do not raise fair value aggressively merely because current asks are high.

Preserve the existing WTrader EMA-based estimator as:

```text
fastEstimate
```

It may contribute to the final model but should not dominate reliable completed-sale history.

## 4. Sales vs Listings

Maintain strict separation:

```text
ASK_PRICE != CONFIRMED_SALE_PRICE
```

Historical confirmed/high-confidence inferred sales should be the strongest evidence for fair value.

Current listings should mainly provide:

```text
competition
market depth
credible ask floor
visible supply
spread
```

Do not train sale-price statistics using every active listing.

